  "summary": "Long-read and genome-resolved metagenomes expose taxa and functions missed by short-read assemblies, alongside new diversity frameworks and cross-habitat surveys.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is resolving microbial community structure and function at finer genomic and phylogenetic resolution across habitats. HiFi long-read metagenomics of activated sludge recovers denitrifiers, nitrifiers and Accumulibacter missed by short-read assemblies, with consequences for N2O interpretation, while Great Barrier Reef sediments yield 2,698 MAGs, mostly novel. hilldiv3 unifies neutral, phylogenetic and functional Hill-number analysis, and MiSA adds statistical detection of spatial dysbiosis in image-based oral biofilm data. Ecological studies contrast patterns: marble subaerial biofilms show taxonomic turnover with conserved phylogenetic structure, octocoral microbiomes are host-specific and stable over three years, and river microeukaryotes track water chemistry. The studies differ in system and method; not all are genome-resolved.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
